1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Fushi learns of Gugu's daily struggles as Hiro tells him about the life he now leads

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
and how Gugu's feelings for Takunaha still run deep.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
I felt like I still had memories to make in Takunaha. I wasn't done yet.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
No matter how much of a paradise you turn this place into, you can't remove people's troubles, doubts, or anguish.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After all, we're only human.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
In a lonely night, we're asking for help.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Can I help you?

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Can I help you with yourself?

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The voice of the heart is ringing.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Let me tell you, let me tell you, let me tell you.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
終わらない想いを繰り返し秘密の彼方へ

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:16,000
不安から遠ざかる術はどこにあるのか見えないまま

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
誰かが変わってくれたなら

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
誰かが変わってくれたなら

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
それで救われるのか

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
不滅のあなたへ叫びたい

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,000
夢動く代わりに歌いたい

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
言葉と言葉を重ねて

19
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
秘密の彼方へ

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
秘密の彼方へ

21
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
秘密の彼方へ

22
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
秘密の彼方へ

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
秘密世界中

24
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
秘密の彼方へ

25
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
秘密世界中

26
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
秘密世界中

27
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,280
Hey, Goo Goo, I can help you with that.

28
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,280
Oh, awesome.

29
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,280
Thank you.

30
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,280
Huh?

31
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,280
I can do it.

32
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:13,760
I can do it.

33
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,880
I got it.

34
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:20,760
Ushii, looks like you're in a good mood today.

35
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:21,760
Mmm.

36
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:35,880
Hey, do you think I'm being silly?

37
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:39,720
I've been trying to get on everyone's good side because I'm worried they'll all leave

38
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:40,720
me.

39
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:43,720
Was that a you got me?

40
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:46,720
Or were you laughing at me?

41
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:51,360
Maybe I'm being crazy for feeling like there's no point in being alive without them.

42
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:54,360
You know, March said something similar a long time ago.

43
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,360
Bon, you're back?

44
00:02:56,360 --> 00:03:01,960
She said she'd be sad, having to live into adulthood without you there by her side.

45
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:06,920
She tried desperately to stop you, but you ignored her and went into a slumber to continue

46
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:07,920
your war.

47
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:10,440
Uh, yeah.

48
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:13,080
So March ingested poison to end it.

49
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,080
Huh?

50
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,520
End it?

51
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:19,080
She took her own life next to you, but she didn't suffer.

52
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:30,760
The city of Renru and its bitter war against the knockers.

53
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:32,080
There were so many casualties.

54
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:39,080
And of course, you'd lost everything too, Fushi.

55
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:45,080
Although, eventually we won.

56
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:52,080
The knockers left the city, and you continued your slumber.

57
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,080
Poor March.

58
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,080
She's just a little girl.

59
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,080
I know what she's going through.

60
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:59,080
It's painful to leave everything behind.

61
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:01,080
It's so hard to move on.

62
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,080
Now listen.

63
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:08,080
I'm the only one who has a good excuse to become a villain here.

64
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:10,080
So tell me what I can do.

65
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:17,080
If I could meet Fushi one more time, you know what I'd say?

66
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:19,080
It's not just physical pain I couldn't get.

67
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:36,080
I also couldn't understand the pains of the soul.

68
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:38,080
the pains of the soul.

69
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:58,080
Hyrule followed through with it.

70
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,080
So did March.

71
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:08,080
Are you leaving, Tanari?

72
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:12,080
I have to. I can't stay here any longer.

73
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,080
Take care of yourself.

74
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:20,080
I'm his big brother. I have to look after his grave.

75
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:26,080
Even long after you'd reacquired your vessels,

76
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:31,080
you were so deep in your slumber that you didn't even recognize us.

77
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:46,080
Toonari was tormented by guilt.

78
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:51,080
She regretted giving March the poison which had allowed her to die.

79
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:57,080
You mustn't let it trouble you. After all, you simply did what needed to be done.

80
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:59,080
Yes, I know. Still…

81
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:03,080
Please understand that I would have done exactly the same if I were in your position.

82
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,080
Fushi will reawaken one day.

83
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:11,080
The Church of Bennett is powerful, and so are the anti-Fushi groups.

84
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:14,080
To them, Fushi is an evil demon,

85
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:18,080
which is all the more reason to spread the word of Fushi the Savior.

86
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,080
Wouldn't you agree?

87
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,080
For the future that lies ahead for everyone.

88
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:27,080
And you're the only one of us who can do it, Tanari.

89
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,080
So Tanari got to work.

90
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,080
She wrote the legend of Fushi.

91
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,080
The truth of Fushi.

92
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:39,080
And then,

93
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:41,080
Hyro spread it all around the world.

94
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,080
However,

95
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:47,080
the anti-Fushi folks were still as aggressive as ever.

96
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:49,080
You're wrong! Fushi isn't like that!

97
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:52,080
He saved this city, and now he's fighting to save the entire world!

98
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,080
Silence! Get him!

99
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,080
Listen, don't fight them!

100
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:57,080
Don't hurt any of them!

101
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,080
Kamu!

102
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:10,080
That's enough!

103
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,080
The King of Sonya!

104
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,080
The throne will now administer this land directly.

105
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:16,080
None shall interfere.

106
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,080
Dammit, Anno, why can you never be on time, huh?

107
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:24,080
Gugu managed to protect your body, never hurting anyone.

108
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:29,080
Massar made sure to keep a watchful eye on the King of Sonya.

109
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:32,080
Although he never cared much for his own well-being,

110
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:35,080
he did bring Euralis and the nation of Sonya together.

111
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,080
Prince Bond!

112
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,080
Apologies, Baron Haramaki.

113
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:41,080
A letter from King Torta for you.

114
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:43,080
Thank you.

115
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:46,080
And through his efforts, Kai brought me and Euralis together.

116
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:52,080
Those Bennett assholes are about to find out what happens when they don't leave us alone.

117
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:56,080
I'm really hoping this is the last time we have to do battle with these people.

118
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,080
Let's go!

119
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:02,080
Our continuous battles against the Bennett territories waged on.

120
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:06,080
Kai and Massar were always there, right on the front lines.

121
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:07,080
Then, around the time the battles ended.

122
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:08,080
I was the last of us to join you.

123
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,080
I was the last of us to join you.

124
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,080
I was the last of us to join you.

125
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,080
I was the last of us to join you.

126
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:13,080
Everyone was waiting for you.

127
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:14,080
For centuries.

128
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:17,080
I was the last of us to join you.

129
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:20,080
Everyone was waiting for you.

130
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:21,080
For centuries.

131
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:35,960
I was the last of us to join you.

132
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:40,300
Everyone was waiting for you, for centuries.

133
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:46,180
And now you're starting to feel that you're going to be the one left behind.

134
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,620
That's just not true.

135
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:51,340
Everyone is trying to live alongside you.

136
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:54,780
Here's something that will blow your immortal mind.

137
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:58,340
Who do you think it was who asked me to come back because they were worried about you?

138
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:00,320
It was Massar. Can you believe that?

139
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:03,160
And here we were, thinking he only cared about booze and girls.

140
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:06,260
Nobody here is so fed up with you that they want to leave this place.

141
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:08,460
In fact, it's quite the opposite. You must know that.

142
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:12,360
If anything, they want you to be happy. Of that, I am absolutely sure.

143
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:16,080
How many times? How many more times?

144
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:19,760
Can we eat together? Talk together? Play together?

145
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:22,880
A thousand? Maybe a hundred more times?

146
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:25,620
How many times will I get to see them again?

147
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:28,020
Plenty of times. As many as you like.

148
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:31,840
You're lying! There will definitely be a last time!

149
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:36,800
I know, because Tanari told me. She said that they're all going to die here.

150
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:44,160
I know the truth. Their only dream is to make their own dreams come true, not to spend their lives living with me forever.

151
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:50,380
Fushi. Whether it's a thousand times or just a hundred, will you ever truly be satisfied?

152
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:53,760
Even if you knew it would be the last time you were together.

153
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:56,300
I couldn't bear that.

154
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:59,400
What's this? Kid's got himself all worked up.

155
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:01,700
Hey, Fushi, are you okay?

156
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:05,100
I just wanted to call you in for dinner.

157
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:07,720
Looks like you're discussing something important.

158
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,520
Yeah, let's go.

159
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:14,200
Fushi, don't you think now's a good time to tell everyone here how you're feeling?

160
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:15,640
What? No way!

161
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:20,680
Hey, come on. What's up?

162
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:25,000
Um, well, let's...

163
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:33,420
Please don't... please don't die and leave me behind.

164
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:42,140
Please don't die and leave you behind? What the hell?

165
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:45,420
It's okay, Fushi. I'll always be here with you.

166
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:47,740
No, that's not what I mean, March.

167
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:49,180
Then what do you mean?

168
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:53,540
Well, for example, if you were to die one day, then as long as you stayed here with me,

169
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:56,920
I wouldn't mind bringing all of you back to life and we can keep on being happy.

170
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:58,300
Seriously?

171
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:03,240
Yeah, like it would be nice to do that. I guess that's what I really mean.

172
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:08,220
So you're asking us to keep living and dying and coming back just like you do? Forever?

173
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:12,160
I'm sorry! I am! Please don't hate me for that!

174
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:16,040
Someone help me with this, please!

175
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:17,400
You're gonna spill it!

176
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,640
And he's gone.

177
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:29,560
Oh, no. Everything I just said to them must have sounded so pathetic.

178
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:33,760
They'll definitely think so little of me now.

179
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:35,960
Why? Why the hell am I...

180
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:37,820
The way I am!

181
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:44,880
I guess none of them understand how I feel because they're not immortal like I am.

182
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:45,940
What did I expect?

183
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,820
What would they do if they were like me?

184
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:56,700
Just who am I supposed to become in this world anyway?

185
00:11:57,480 --> 00:12:00,780
I mean, I should figure out who I want to become like...

186
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:03,680
Oh, did you come to get me again?

187
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,760
It's okay. You don't need to worry about me.

188
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,780
Wasn't this where...

189
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:22,260
Oh, are these all the babies from the eggs I laid?

190
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:25,280
I can't believe each one of them has a pie!

191
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:26,440
Amazing!

192
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:28,340
I'm a mom now, too!

193
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:29,480
Oh, right!

194
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:30,980
I should give you all names!

195
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,300
You're called Shumai,

196
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:33,200
you're Gyoza,

197
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:33,840
Ramen,

198
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,080
Twice Cooked Pork,

199
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:35,880
Chop Suey!

200
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:39,240
I promise I'll give you a name someday, too, horse.

201
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:41,860
Where are you going?

202
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:43,860
To the sea?

203
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:44,900
But wait!

204
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,500
I've only just found you!

205
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:49,680
What are you doing,

206
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:50,880
evil crabs?

207
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,000
Stop it!

208
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,880
You can't eat Shumai!

209
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:03,100
Everyone, come here!

210
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:04,380
It's too dangerous outside!

211
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:05,780
I'll protect you!

212
00:13:05,780 --> 00:13:08,720
We can all go home and live together forever!

213
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,900
That'll be much better for you!

214
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,180
I'm sorry!

215
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:16,960
Please, tell me you don't hate me!

216
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:19,160
Don't hate me!

217
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:21,580
I couldn't stand it if you did!

218
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:34,580
Everyone...

219
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:37,500
was so very kind.

220
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:42,680
Right to the end!

221
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:42,700
Right to the end!

222
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:43,200
...

223
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:43,360
I don't like a secret...

224
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:43,900
...

225
00:13:47,220 --> 00:13:48,520
Nice to meet you!

226
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:49,580
I don't like it!

227
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:57,120
I'm sorry...

228
00:13:57,120 --> 00:14:00,140
...

229
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:02,740
I'm sorry...

230
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:20,740
I'm FUNA!

231
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:26,740
Huh? Hang on! What the hell?

232
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:32,740
Oh, wow! Fushi, your new hairstyle looks great on you!

233
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:36,740
Ah, and I see Mizua is absent again.

234
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:44,740
Yeah, you can do it!

235
00:14:52,740 --> 00:14:55,740
What?! Cherry Blossom viewing at the VP's house?!

236
00:14:55,740 --> 00:15:00,740
Sounds good to me. Does this mean that we also get the opportunity to meet your other friends as well, Fushi?

237
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:02,740
Yeah, of course, right? Fushi?

238
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:03,740
Mm-hmm.

239
00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:06,740
Looks like we're going to have quite the crowd.

240
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,740
Hey, you should come too.

241
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:09,740
I'd love to.

242
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:11,740
Something wrong?

243
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:13,740
Oh, um...

244
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,740
No, it's nothing.

245
00:15:20,740 --> 00:15:22,740
Need detergent? I can get it.

246
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:24,740
Oh, not that one. Get the bottle instead.

247
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:27,740
Oh, perfect. That's the one.

248
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:33,740
You know, you're pretty good at this, Fushi.

249
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:35,740
Well, Goo Goo taught me a long time ago.

250
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:38,740
Wow, you've improved so much!

251
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:41,740
Well, let's talk about the next Bonest Award.

252
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:43,740
It's my opinion that it should go to...

253
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:49,740
Fushi sure does sleep a lot. Especially on the weekends.

254
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:52,740
Seems like he's been working really hard lately.

255
00:15:52,740 --> 00:16:03,740
Tenori! The bag's ready!

256
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:05,740
Eko, why don't you join us?

257
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:07,740
We'll be back halfway with the announcements!

258
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:08,740
Hey guys, we're all getting ready to go to bed.

259
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:09,740
Okay, yeah.

260
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:14,740
By the way, Goo Goo, I wanted to give you this.

261
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:15,740
Huh?

262
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:17,740
Oh, what is it?

263
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:19,740
It's a ticket to Takunaha.

264
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:22,740
Huh? To Takunaha?

265
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:24,740
What brought this on?

266
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:26,740
How'd you manage to get it?

267
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:28,740
I saved up and bought it.

268
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:31,740
I left an empty shell here and went to earn money.

269
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:32,740
I worked at a restaurant.

270
00:16:32,740 --> 00:16:35,740
You're young, but you're so good!

271
00:16:35,740 --> 00:16:38,740
Wait, you worked a job and saved up all for me?

272
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:41,740
Mm-hmm. You should go during spring break.

273
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:44,740
Damn! This is so awesome, man!

274
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:45,740
I can't believe it!

275
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:46,740
Thank you so much!

276
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:49,740
Oh, crap! I can't just be standing around!

277
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:50,740
I've gotta go pack!

278
00:16:50,740 --> 00:16:54,740
I wonder if our plugs will work with the outlets over there.

279
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:56,740
Hey, Fushi, you got a phone?

280
00:16:56,740 --> 00:16:57,740
Uh-oh.

281
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:58,740
You should buy one.

282
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:00,740
Also, do you have any light jackets you can take?

283
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:03,740
I can lend you one of mine if you don't.

284
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:04,740
No, because...

285
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:05,740
Oh, that's right.

286
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:07,740
I guess you don't need to pack anything.

287
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:09,740
You'll be waiting for me over there.

288
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:11,740
I'm not going, Gugu.

289
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:16,740
I wanted you to be able to live over there for as long as you like.

290
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:19,740
I asked Kazumitsu and Bond to get permission from the school.

291
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:21,740
Oh.

292
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:23,740
So that's what this is.

293
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:25,740
You sure you're okay with this?

294
00:17:25,740 --> 00:17:28,740
You're not gonna get all mopey again, are you?

295
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:29,740
No, I won't.

296
00:17:29,740 --> 00:17:31,740
I promise, brother.

297
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:40,740
No, Hyrule.

298
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:42,740
Please don't graduate and leave us all.

299
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:43,740
Above all, don't get a girlfriend.

300
00:17:43,740 --> 00:17:44,740
Hey.

301
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:45,740
Well done graduating.

302
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:50,740
I bet you're not happy graduating when you're this popular, right?

303
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:52,740
Yeah, kinda.

304
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:55,740
It was an interesting place for me, and I admit, I'm gonna miss it.

305
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:58,740
But it's not even close to how much I'm gonna miss you, Gugu.

306
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:00,740
You can cut that shit out!

307
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:02,740
You know how much I can't stand all that sentimental stuff!

308
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:03,740
Gugu!

309
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:04,740
Come on now!

310
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:05,740
He just healed!

311
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:11,740
You're gonna make sure you come back once a year, right?

312
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:15,740
But we're really going to miss you, so I think you should come back once a week instead.

313
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:16,740
Right, Fushi?

314
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:19,740
I don't think something like that's going to be very doable, March.

315
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:20,740
Really?

316
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:23,740
I tell you what, I'll do my best to come back whenever I can.

317
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:26,740
I brought more tea in case anybody wants some.

318
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:27,740
Hey there, Yuki.

319
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:28,740
Thanks so much for inviting us.

320
00:18:28,740 --> 00:18:29,740
Hi, VP.

321
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:32,740
Hello and welcome, fellow Occult Club members.

322
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:33,740
Handicrafts Club.

323
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:34,740
Very nice to meet you.

324
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:35,740
I'm Hana.

325
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:36,740
Hello there.

326
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:38,740
Thank you very much for having us.

327
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:40,740
Wow, so this is the Vice President's place?

328
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:42,740
Is that horse free range?

329
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:45,740
It's a good thing the flowers bloom during spring break this year.

330
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:46,740
Perfect time, wouldn't you say?

331
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:47,740
I agree.

332
00:18:47,740 --> 00:18:49,740
Hey, come sit and join us.

333
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:50,740
I'd love to.

334
00:18:50,740 --> 00:18:51,740
Thanks.

335
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:52,740
Hi there.

336
00:18:52,740 --> 00:18:53,740
What are you making?

337
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:56,740
Tasty... dumplings?

338
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:59,740
Yeah, tasty.

339
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:02,740
You're really good at making dumplings, aren't you?

340
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:05,740
Hey, is there something wrong?

341
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:07,740
Look at this.

342
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:09,740
My youngest child's name is Kanitaro.

343
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:11,740
Wow, what an amazing crab.

344
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:13,740
Did you raise him yourself?

345
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:14,740
Yep.

346
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:15,740
I'm his mommy.

347
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:16,740
Oh, wow.

348
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:19,740
So if you're his mom, then can I be his dad?

349
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:21,740
Oh, of course.

350
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:24,740
Come on, let's go make a house over here.

351
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:25,740
Hello.

352
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:28,740
Are you Gugu by any chance?

353
00:19:28,740 --> 00:19:30,740
The VP told us all about you.

354
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:32,740
Is it true that you can breathe fire?

355
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:33,740
Ugh.

356
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:38,740
Can we have your autograph?

357
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:41,740
I wish Mizuha could be here.

358
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,740
She would've had fun.

359
00:19:43,740 --> 00:19:46,740
I hope she's okay.

360
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:48,740
I mean, she hasn't even been to school lately, huh?

361
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:49,740
Yeah.

362
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:52,740
Nah, it's not all bad.

363
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:55,740
Sometimes absence makes the heart grow fonder.

364
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:56,740
What?

365
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:59,740
We all talking about Gugu, ain't that right?

366
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:00,740
Ah.

367
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:04,740
The Tsar, if you're going to smoke around people, then you need to learn proper etiquette.

368
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:08,740
Why don't you use this before Kazumitsu yells at you again?

369
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:10,740
Uh, what the hell is this, an ashtray?

370
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:11,740
Yep.

371
00:20:11,740 --> 00:20:13,740
Wait, did you like make this or something?

372
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:15,740
Yeah, it's a gift for you.

373
00:20:15,740 --> 00:20:17,740
What do you mean by that?

374
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:24,740
I'm planning on taking an apprenticeship with a blacksmith, but for now I'm going to focus on making things like these instead of swords.

375
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:25,740
Good luck, Kai.

376
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:26,740
You got this.

377
00:20:26,740 --> 00:20:28,740
Ah, that's right.

378
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:29,740
Whoa!

379
00:20:29,740 --> 00:20:31,740
You're really giving this to me?

380
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:32,740
Thanks so much, Masar.

381
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:34,740
That's such a nice gift.

382
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:36,740
I have something for you too, Hyro.

383
00:20:36,740 --> 00:20:37,740
What?

384
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:38,740
You're giving me this bike?

385
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:39,740
Yeah.

386
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:40,740
You wanted one, right?

387
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,740
That's so kind of you, Masar.

388
00:20:42,740 --> 00:20:46,740
Nah, I just happened to went at the horse track and did a little shopping, that's all.

389
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:47,740
Come on, I had it.

390
00:20:47,740 --> 00:20:48,740
Over here.

391
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:49,740
Don't.

392
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:50,740
We'll set it, yeah.

393
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:51,740
Right.

394
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:56,740
You didn't have to see me off, you know.

395
00:20:56,740 --> 00:20:58,740
Could've just stayed at home and chilled.

396
00:20:58,740 --> 00:20:59,740
No way.

397
00:20:59,740 --> 00:21:00,740
I couldn't have done that.

398
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:01,740
Oh, hey.

399
00:21:01,740 --> 00:21:03,740
Have you ever tried these before?

400
00:21:03,740 --> 00:21:04,740
Mm-mm.

401
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:05,740
They're great.

402
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:07,740
You should get Bond to buy them.

403
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:08,740
Hmph.

404
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:12,740
If I had any money, I would've bought you plenty of things.

405
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:15,740
I never got to do any Big Brother stuff for you.

406
00:21:15,740 --> 00:21:17,740
It's fine, you know that.

407
00:21:24,740 --> 00:21:26,740
Okay, I'm good from here, Fushi.

408
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:27,740
Mm.

409
00:21:27,740 --> 00:21:31,740
We're gonna be really far apart for quite a while.

410
00:21:31,740 --> 00:21:32,740
I know.

411
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:34,740
One day, we'll see each other again.

412
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:35,740
Hmph.

413
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:36,740
Ha!

414
00:21:36,740 --> 00:21:38,740
Well, no kidding, right?

415
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:42,740
You can make it to Takunaha in less than ten seconds, can't you, Fushi?

416
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:43,740
Ha!

417
00:21:43,740 --> 00:21:47,740
Well, anyway, for real though, you're always welcome to come hang out.

418
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:50,740
Yeah, I'll try my best to hold back though.

419
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:52,740
I feel like that's for the best.

420
00:21:52,740 --> 00:21:54,740
Yeah, I get it.

421
00:21:54,740 --> 00:21:56,740
I'll be rooting for you from Takunaha.

422
00:21:56,740 --> 00:21:58,740
Please make your way to gate 47.

423
00:21:58,740 --> 00:21:59,740
See you later.

424
00:21:59,740 --> 00:22:02,740
Let me know as soon as you buy a smartphone, okay?

425
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:03,740
I'll get one now.

426
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:11,740
By the way, how do planes even fly?

427
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:12,740
I don't get it.

428
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:13,740
It looks impossible.

429
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:14,740
Scary.

430
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:17,740
I could never see myself riding in one of those things.

431
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:18,740
Weren't you afraid, Gugu?

432
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:20,740
You were scared?

433
00:22:20,740 --> 00:22:22,740
You can literally turn into a bird.

434
00:22:22,740 --> 00:22:24,740
You'll just have to get used to this stuff.

435
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:28,740
Who knows what kind of vehicles people will have in a hundred or a thousand years from now.

436
00:22:28,740 --> 00:22:32,740
It's important to keep up with civilization.

437
00:22:32,740 --> 00:22:34,740
For you and me both.

438
00:22:38,740 --> 00:22:43,740
Happy birthday to me.

439
00:22:43,740 --> 00:22:48,740
Happy birthday to me.

440
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:55,740
Happy birthday dear Mizuha.

441
00:22:55,740 --> 00:22:56,740
Happy birthday.

442
00:22:56,740 --> 00:22:59,740
Happy birthday.

443
00:22:59,740 --> 00:23:02,740
Happy birthday birthdayל

444
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:07,740
Happy birthday

445
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:09,740
Happy birthday!

446
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:12,740
Happy birthday!

447
00:23:12,740 --> 00:23:13,740
Happy birthday!

448
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:23,740
Happy birthday!

449
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:53,720
We'll be right back.

450
00:23:53,740 --> 00:24:23,720
We'll be right back.

451
00:24:23,740 --> 00:24:53,720
We'll be right back.

452
00:24:53,740 --> 00:25:23,720
We'll be right back.

